  "remaining": [
    "VECTOR.SILU_MUL is now 67.8% of the decode token and ATTENTION.GQA 11.8%: both wait on one correctly rounded exponential per element (~2,900 cycles each). That is datapath: a faster certified exp or several interleaved units, not control.",
    "the span-16 prefill gains only 1.066x (103,107,755 -> 96,753,768 cycles): the scatter saving is the same ~6.35 M cycles, and the rest of prefill was not profiled here; with 16 query rows its SiLU and attention exponentials are 16x the decode count, so it is expected to be even more exponential-bound",
    "the admission bridge (~33 cycles per issue of serial descriptor reads) and the front end (RESOLVE ~17 cycles per issue) could be prefetched ahead of the wait set; measured at ~72 cycles per issue, 0.09% of the new token, it is not worth the bridge risk on this workload",
    "vector walks (RMS, head-RMS, RoPE, ADD at 8.6-12.3 cycles per element; ARGMAX at 3) are issue-wait-use loops like the old mover: ~46 k cycles, 0.7% of the new token",
    "clock: the vehicle is bounded by datapath blocks (qwen_gqa 69.7 MHz not met, fp32_div_rne 283.5, transcendental 306.8); the bridge, device top and engine array have no routed record"
  ]
